---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Systems and project availability
description: Explore ForgeWire Labs software and research with distinct ownership, architecture, source links, and honest release boundaries.
permalink: /projects/index.html
---
<section class="page-lead page-shell" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Field notes / 02 · Project register</p>
  <h1 id="projects-title">A portfolio of systems with <em>separate jobs and release states.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead-copy">The projects span repository governance, planning, communication, distributed execution, and structured learning. Their links, diagrams, and availability labels point to the source that owns each claim.</p>
  <p class="lead-index"><span>Public releases</span><span>Source-build previews</span><span>Private development</span></p>
</section>

<section class="repository-spread page-shell" aria-labelledby="repopact-title">
  <div class="spread-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 / ForgeWire Labs · Repository systems</p>
    <h2 id="repopact-title">RepoPact</h2>
    <p>Core defines and validates governed repository state. Workbench is a separate native interface that consumes Core and carries its own preview status.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="repo-product-grid">
    {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "repopact-core" or project.id == "repopact-workbench" %}
      <article class="product-entry product-entry--{{ project.statusKind }}" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
        <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
        <h3><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3>
        <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
        <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Availability.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
        <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% if project.secondaryUrl %}<a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endif %}</div>
      </article>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
  <div class="repo-evidence-grid">
    <figure class="architecture-figure architecture-figure--page">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/repopact-architecture.svg" alt="RepoPact Core architecture diagram. Repository records are authoritative; the Rust engine interprets and validates them, CLI and Workbench clients use that engine, derived views remain secondary, and optional integrations have limited boundaries." width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>Architecture from the <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-core/blob/614689b127cf52f801877cc48440f7e45c3709eb/docs/assets/readme/repopact-architecture.svg">RepoPact Core repository</a>. Source records stay authoritative; interface views do not.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="screenshot-figure">
      <div class="screenshot-frame screenshot-frame--light"><img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg" alt="Genuine Windows x64 desktop capture of RepoPact Workbench showing repository validation and navigation for Work, Decisions, Evidence, Graph, and Analysis." width="2880" height="1800" loading="lazy"></div>
      <figcaption><strong>Workbench, source-build preview.</strong> This genuine capture is documented in the project's README as a local build using a disposable Core conformance fixture. Packaged installers are not listed. <a href="https://github.com/ForgeWireLabs/repopact-workbench/blob/414a4a78091796735a1b97b03fd8c3cf1c105f30/docs/assets/readme/workbench-desktop-dashboard.jpg">View the source image and provenance ↗</a></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="private-section" aria-labelledby="private-title">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <div class="private-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Research and private development</p>
      <h2 id="private-title">Work can be architecturally important before it is available.</h2>
      <p>The public materials describe direction and status. No public build or supported deployment is available for these projects.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="private-register">
      {% for project in projects %}{% if project.group == "private" %}
        <article class="private-record" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
          <p class="eyebrow">{{ project.kicker }}</p>
          <h3>{% if project.url %}<a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% else %}{{ project.name }}{% endif %}</h3>
          <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
          <p class="availability-copy"><strong>{{ project.status }}.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
          {% if project.url %}<a class="text-link" href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endif %}
        </article>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="planning-spread page-shell" aria-labelledby="anvil-title">
  <div class="planning-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">03 / ForgeWire Labs · Planning</p>
    <p class="spread-number" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
  </div>
  {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "anvil" %}
    <article class="planning-entry" data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
      <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
      <h2 id="anvil-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
      <p class="planning-summary">{{ project.summary }}</p>
      <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Boundary.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </article>
  {% endif %}{% endfor %}
</section>

<section class="communication-section" aria-labelledby="forgelink-title">
  <div class="page-shell communication-layout">
    <div class="communication-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Related work · JeremyShows</p>
      {% for project in projects %}{% if project.id == "forgelink" %}
        <div data-project-id="{{ project.id }}">
          <div class="product-entry-top"><span>{{ project.kicker }}</span><span class="status status--{{ project.statusKind }}">{{ project.status }}</span></div>
          <h2 id="forgelink-title"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.name }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h2>
          <p>{{ project.summary }}</p>
          <p class="availability-copy"><strong>Ownership and release.</strong> {{ project.maturity }}</p>
          <div class="product-entry-links"><a href="{{ project.url }}">{{ project.action }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="{{ project.secondaryUrl }}">{{ project.secondaryAction }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </div>
      {% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
    <figure class="forgelink-figure">
      <img src="{{ site.basePath }}/assets/forgelink-product-architecture.svg" alt="ForgeLink architecture from its separate JeremyShows repository. The human operator uses the communication cockpit; agents enter through governed APIs, while providers and ForgeWire or Fabric remain optional edges." width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy">
      <figcaption>The project’s own architecture diagram. ForgeLink is related work maintained under JeremyShows, outside the ForgeWire Labs organization.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="learning-section page-shell" aria-labelledby="skillforge-title">
